WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.374 --> 00:00:02.923
- If it's the right person
telling me not to do something,

00:00:02.923 --> 00:00:05.112
I go, "Oh, I got something here."

00:00:05.112 --> 00:00:07.231
It's like Jay-Z said it best, like,

00:00:07.231 --> 00:00:09.372
make your first your last.

00:00:09.372 --> 00:00:10.729
Everything you do you have to do it

00:00:10.729 --> 00:00:12.349
like it's the last thing
you're ever going to do.

00:00:12.349 --> 00:00:14.082
You know, some guys watch stuff and go,

00:00:14.082 --> 00:00:16.110
"I want to do a movie like that."

00:00:16.110 --> 00:00:18.935
And I watch movies and I go,
"Okay, I don't want to do that

00:00:18.935 --> 00:00:20.003
"'cause I saw it."

00:00:20.003 --> 00:00:22.257
I'm just trying to do the best work I can,

00:00:22.257 --> 00:00:25.273
work that I can be proud of later on.

00:00:25.273 --> 00:00:27.025
When I see this thing play
in front of an audience,

00:00:27.025 --> 00:00:28.300
people go crazy.

00:00:28.300 --> 00:00:29.523
AT every point of my life,

00:00:29.523 --> 00:00:34.277
there's no point where I
wasn't obsessed with comedy.

00:00:34.277 --> 00:00:36.631
You can't make a woman happy.

00:00:36.631 --> 00:00:38.597
It's impossible.

00:00:38.597 --> 00:00:41.345
I've never met a happy woman in my life.

00:00:41.345 --> 00:00:44.260
- He's an American comedian,
actor, and producer.

00:00:44.260 --> 00:00:45.455
After working as a stand up comic,

00:00:45.455 --> 00:00:46.960
he came to wider prominence

00:00:46.960 --> 00:00:49.754
as a cast member of Saturday Night Live.

00:00:49.754 --> 00:00:52.087
He was voted as the fifth
greatest stand up comedian

00:00:52.087 --> 00:00:54.837
of all time by a poll by Comedy Central.

00:00:54.837 --> 00:00:56.646
He's Chris Rock and here's my take

00:00:56.646 --> 00:00:58.688
on his top ten rules for success.

00:00:58.688 --> 00:01:00.632
Number six is my personal favorite

00:01:00.632 --> 00:01:02.552
and make sure to stick
around all the way to the end

00:01:02.552 --> 00:01:04.635
for some special bonuses.

00:01:07.793 --> 00:01:08.999
- You know, people try to tell you

00:01:08.999 --> 00:01:10.335
not to say things all the time.

00:01:10.335 --> 00:01:13.511
But, you know, I practice everything.

00:01:13.511 --> 00:01:14.826
It's not like I ever get up there

00:01:14.826 --> 00:01:16.430
and think of something on stage

00:01:16.430 --> 00:01:18.420
or think of something on T.V.

00:01:18.420 --> 00:01:21.242
I'm pretty much, you know, trying it out.

00:01:21.242 --> 00:01:22.075
- [Interviewer] Yeah.

00:01:22.075 --> 00:01:26.018
- And honestly, sometimes,
if it's the right person

00:01:26.018 --> 00:01:27.635
telling me not to do something,

00:01:27.635 --> 00:01:29.687
I go, "Oh, I got something here."

00:01:29.687 --> 00:01:30.839
You know what I mean, like,

00:01:30.839 --> 00:01:32.116
"Oh, you don't like it?

00:01:32.116 --> 00:01:33.927
"It must be good."

00:01:33.927 --> 00:01:35.538
- There's a benchmark,
you've set a high benchmark,

00:01:35.538 --> 00:01:37.252
certainly where the stand up
is concerned, a high benchmark.

00:01:37.252 --> 00:01:40.732
How do you keep pushing past that line?

00:01:40.732 --> 00:01:43.175
- I mean, it's almost like every,

00:01:43.175 --> 00:01:44.884
it's like Jay-Z said it best,

00:01:44.884 --> 00:01:47.171
like, make your first your last.

00:01:47.171 --> 00:01:48.809
Everything you do you have to do it

00:01:48.809 --> 00:01:50.666
like it's the last thing
you're ever going to do.

00:01:50.666 --> 00:01:54.583
And, you know, to get
maximum effort out of it.

00:01:56.775 --> 00:02:00.108
But it also goes, when
you start something,

00:02:00.108 --> 00:02:02.476
it's almost like it has to be a calling.

00:02:02.476 --> 00:02:05.640
Again, you know, like, you
know, we're all like preachers.

00:02:05.640 --> 00:02:07.402
I was called into stand up.

00:02:07.402 --> 00:02:09.238
I was called into comedy.

00:02:09.238 --> 00:02:12.355
And, you know, I just, the next
project has to be something

00:02:12.355 --> 00:02:13.886
that just calls me.

00:02:13.886 --> 00:02:14.719
You know what I mean?

00:02:14.719 --> 00:02:18.536
I'm a decent business man, you know,

00:02:18.536 --> 00:02:20.953
but, I just really have to be

00:02:22.394 --> 00:02:24.637
emotionally attached to something.

00:02:24.637 --> 00:02:26.723
- Before I leave your early life,

00:02:26.723 --> 00:02:29.285
I also heard that you went to a school

00:02:29.285 --> 00:02:33.176
that was out of your
initial neighborhood and--

00:02:33.176 --> 00:02:34.009
- Yeah, I was bussed.

00:02:34.009 --> 00:02:35.244
I was bussed to school.

00:02:35.244 --> 00:02:38.411
It was pretty, you know, whatever man.

00:02:39.478 --> 00:02:42.806
People, you know, were mean
and they called you nigger

00:02:42.806 --> 00:02:46.316
and whatever and spit
on you and threw feces

00:02:46.316 --> 00:02:49.134
and piss and whatever at you.

00:02:49.134 --> 00:02:51.772
And, you know, it is what it is.

00:02:51.772 --> 00:02:52.989
There's nothing I can do about it.

00:02:52.989 --> 00:02:54.656
It made me stronger.

00:02:56.332 --> 00:02:58.332
I'm not here without it.

00:03:00.722 --> 00:03:04.639
You can't phase me with
meanness because of it.

00:03:05.711 --> 00:03:09.878
So, you know, that was my
grade school experience,

00:03:11.560 --> 00:03:13.546
grade school, high school,
junior high school.

00:03:13.546 --> 00:03:16.796
- And what inspired this story for you?

00:03:17.840 --> 00:03:18.673
- I don't know.

00:03:18.673 --> 00:03:21.969
I just wanted, I'm always,
my interest is always like,

00:03:21.969 --> 00:03:24.360
what haven't I seen?

00:03:24.360 --> 00:03:26.311
You know, some guys watch stuff and go,

00:03:26.311 --> 00:03:28.362
"I want to do a movie like that."

00:03:28.362 --> 00:03:29.523
And I watch movies and I go,

00:03:29.523 --> 00:03:32.213
"Okay, I don't want to
do that 'cause I saw it."

00:03:32.213 --> 00:03:33.636
Now what can I come up with?

00:03:33.636 --> 00:03:35.117
And I haven't seen this movie.

00:03:35.117 --> 00:03:35.950
- [Interviewer] Yeah.

00:03:35.950 --> 00:03:36.783
- You know, and I really haven't

00:03:36.783 --> 00:03:38.039
seen this movie with a black person.

00:03:38.039 --> 00:03:38.872
You know what I mean?

00:03:38.872 --> 00:03:40.768
So, that's me.

00:03:40.768 --> 00:03:43.366
It gets me into trouble sometimes,

00:03:43.366 --> 00:03:45.944
but I'm just kind of curious that way.

00:03:45.944 --> 00:03:48.852
Like, okay, can we see a new movie?

00:03:48.852 --> 00:03:49.909
- How do you personally navigate it?

00:03:49.909 --> 00:03:51.674
Is it really that easy
for you, that simple?

00:03:51.674 --> 00:03:52.869
You crack a joke and keep moving?

00:03:52.869 --> 00:03:53.819
- I just keep moving.

00:03:53.819 --> 00:03:55.952
Here's the thing with me,

00:03:55.952 --> 00:03:59.858
I don't take the adulation that serious.

00:03:59.858 --> 00:04:03.275
Because if I put, you know, if, you know,

00:04:05.429 --> 00:04:07.224
The New York Times says,
"Oh, he's a genius."

00:04:07.224 --> 00:04:09.619
And I just run around
going, "I'm a genius!

00:04:09.619 --> 00:04:12.109
"The New York Times says I'm a genius!"

00:04:12.109 --> 00:04:16.253
Then if they say I'm an
idiot, I got to say that, too.

00:04:16.253 --> 00:04:17.223
(laughing)

00:04:17.223 --> 00:04:18.981
That has to be important to me, too.

00:04:18.981 --> 00:04:23.199
So, I find that if I don't
pay attention to any of it,

00:04:23.199 --> 00:04:25.738
then I can ignore the bad stuff.

00:04:25.738 --> 00:04:26.571
That's me.

00:04:26.571 --> 00:04:30.173
A lot of people take the
criticism more to heart.

00:04:30.173 --> 00:04:33.326
I just worry about my fans, that's it.

00:04:33.326 --> 00:04:35.919
That's the only people I'm worried about.

00:04:35.919 --> 00:04:36.842
- You say worry about your fans.

00:04:36.842 --> 00:04:37.887
You mean by that, what?

00:04:37.887 --> 00:04:41.183
- I'm just concerned
with what my fans feel.

00:04:41.183 --> 00:04:42.702
Like, how do they feel about the art?

00:04:42.702 --> 00:04:44.322
How do they feel about the movie?

00:04:44.322 --> 00:04:46.395
How do they feel about
just me as a person?

00:04:46.395 --> 00:04:48.387
The people that are into me,

00:04:48.387 --> 00:04:50.625
not the people that aren't into me.

00:04:50.625 --> 00:04:51.458
You know what I mean?

00:04:51.458 --> 00:04:54.672
Like, I don't listen to country music.

00:04:54.672 --> 00:04:58.435
So I am not qualified to say, you know,

00:04:58.435 --> 00:05:00.408
the Travis Tritt album is not good.

00:05:00.408 --> 00:05:01.445
(laughing)

00:05:01.445 --> 00:05:03.980
So I think only people that are your fans

00:05:03.980 --> 00:05:05.555
can be your critics.

00:05:05.555 --> 00:05:06.778
You know what I mean?
- Right.

00:05:06.778 --> 00:05:09.521
You know, I could maybe say
a Prince album I don't like,

00:05:09.521 --> 00:05:10.683
but there are none.

00:05:10.683 --> 00:05:11.678
You know what I mean?

00:05:11.678 --> 00:05:13.680
Because I listen to Prince.

00:05:13.680 --> 00:05:15.263
So, yeah, I'm fine.

00:05:16.579 --> 00:05:18.436
- But you've awesome said that Top Five

00:05:18.436 --> 00:05:20.471
is a kind of make or break movie

00:05:20.471 --> 00:05:22.807
because you've written
it, you've directed it,

00:05:22.807 --> 00:05:24.809
as well as being in it.

00:05:24.809 --> 00:05:26.573
I mean, you could have chosen

00:05:26.573 --> 00:05:29.228
the predictable path, couldn't you?

00:05:29.228 --> 00:05:31.920
And just have taken your
comedy and gotten bigger

00:05:31.920 --> 00:05:33.913
and bigger and bigger, but you haven't.

00:05:33.913 --> 00:05:38.824
- I mean, I could've done
something more contrived.

00:05:38.824 --> 00:05:42.806
Yes, I could have done something
where my partner is killed.

00:05:42.806 --> 00:05:45.550
I'm a cop and they killed my partner

00:05:45.550 --> 00:05:48.759
and I have to get revenge on
the killers of my partner.

00:05:48.759 --> 00:05:52.055
I could have done that
movie, which everybody does.

00:05:52.055 --> 00:05:53.870
And it probably would've
been bigger than Top Five,

00:05:53.870 --> 00:05:55.826
(laughs) honestly.

00:05:55.826 --> 00:05:58.081
But it wouldn't have been better.

00:05:58.081 --> 00:05:58.985
It wouldn't be better.

00:05:58.985 --> 00:06:00.402
So, I don't know.

00:06:01.664 --> 00:06:04.328
I'm just trying to do the best work I can,

00:06:04.328 --> 00:06:07.420
work that I can be proud of later on,

00:06:07.420 --> 00:06:10.775
work that works on different levels.

00:06:10.775 --> 00:06:12.881
You know, a good movie or a good stand up

00:06:12.881 --> 00:06:15.963
is different every time you watch it.

00:06:15.963 --> 00:06:17.510
- I was wondering, how
important was it for you

00:06:17.510 --> 00:06:19.999
to get this large ensemble of, you know,

00:06:19.999 --> 00:06:21.998
your friends, these
very talented comedians,

00:06:21.998 --> 00:06:23.889
these new comedians, as well.

00:06:23.889 --> 00:06:26.146
You know, why was that
important for you to do--

00:06:26.146 --> 00:06:30.313
- It was just important to get
the best people in the parts.

00:06:31.316 --> 00:06:32.452
That was pretty much it.

00:06:32.452 --> 00:06:36.220
I mean, and it's hard to
make comedy with strangers.

00:06:36.220 --> 00:06:38.072
So, you got to know people.

00:06:38.072 --> 00:06:40.405
So, you know, I know Cedric.

00:06:41.770 --> 00:06:43.278
So I know that part of him.

00:06:43.278 --> 00:06:45.562
I know that gritty part
of Cedric the Entertainer

00:06:45.562 --> 00:06:47.541
that everybody else might not know.

00:06:47.541 --> 00:06:48.374
- You want some of the syrup?

00:06:48.374 --> 00:06:49.207
- No, no, I'm good.

00:06:49.207 --> 00:06:51.385
- Good, 'cause I'm the
(beep) man in Houston, man.

00:06:51.385 --> 00:06:52.449
I'm going to tell you that right now.

00:06:52.449 --> 00:06:54.437
I'm the (beep) man in Houston, baby.

00:06:54.437 --> 00:06:56.963
- I know that J.B.'s a, you know,

00:06:56.963 --> 00:06:58.363
been married for like 20 years

00:06:58.363 --> 00:06:59.769
and he's got a couple daughters.

00:06:59.769 --> 00:07:02.232
And I know he can be
like a calming influence,

00:07:02.232 --> 00:07:04.029
where most times you see J.B. in a movie,

00:07:04.029 --> 00:07:06.079
he's a crazy guy!

00:07:06.079 --> 00:07:07.414
- Oh, I love me a thick girl.

00:07:07.414 --> 00:07:08.678
You moving with confidence!

00:07:08.678 --> 00:07:10.234
- I ain't got time for your (beep), Silk.

00:07:10.234 --> 00:07:11.162
I'm seeing somebody.

00:07:11.162 --> 00:07:11.995
- Ain't no problem.

00:07:11.995 --> 00:07:12.828
Come on.

00:07:12.828 --> 00:07:14.488
- You don't get the (beep) out my face.

00:07:14.488 --> 00:07:17.321
- So, you know, I know this about,

00:07:18.473 --> 00:07:21.156
it's easier to work with
people you know sometimes.

00:07:21.156 --> 00:07:22.220
- You're happy with it, though?

00:07:22.220 --> 00:07:23.095
- I'm real happy with it.

00:07:23.095 --> 00:07:25.173
When I see this thing play
in front of an audience,

00:07:25.173 --> 00:07:26.334
people go crazy.

00:07:26.334 --> 00:07:27.167
- Yeah.

00:07:27.167 --> 00:07:28.474
What's you, is there one of those

00:07:28.474 --> 00:07:30.040
Inside the Actor's Studio questions.

00:07:30.040 --> 00:07:34.150
So what's your process, once you do this.

00:07:34.150 --> 00:07:36.056
You want to watch it with other audiences?

00:07:36.056 --> 00:07:37.033
You don't want to see it?

00:07:37.033 --> 00:07:37.988
You study this thing?

00:07:37.988 --> 00:07:40.520
What's your process once they
say "cut" and that's a wrap?

00:07:40.520 --> 00:07:42.049
- You know, you cut it, you know,

00:07:42.049 --> 00:07:43.335
you got to watch it with an audience.

00:07:43.335 --> 00:07:44.332
It's not drama.

00:07:44.332 --> 00:07:45.165
- [Interviewer] Right.

00:07:45.165 --> 00:07:47.927
- Drama is whatever you want it to be.

00:07:47.927 --> 00:07:51.498
When you make drama, you are like Picasso.

00:07:51.498 --> 00:07:53.490
And it's like, "Okay, whatever."

00:07:53.490 --> 00:07:57.840
When you make comedy, you're
not that kind of painter.

00:07:57.840 --> 00:07:59.322
You're like a painter
down at the promenade

00:07:59.322 --> 00:08:01.019
painting portraits to people.

00:08:01.019 --> 00:08:03.084
You know, so, "Oh, you want
more blue in your eyes?

00:08:03.084 --> 00:08:04.229
"I'm going to put more blue in your eyes."

00:08:04.229 --> 00:08:05.142
(laughing)

00:08:05.142 --> 00:08:06.417
"You want to be taller?

00:08:06.417 --> 00:08:08.025
"Okay, you're taller."

00:08:08.025 --> 00:08:10.079
You know, I'm one of those guys.

00:08:10.079 --> 00:08:10.912
- Right.

00:08:10.912 --> 00:08:11.745
- That's so, when you make comedy,

00:08:11.745 --> 00:08:13.078
you make it for the people.

00:08:13.078 --> 00:08:15.729
You know, you try to
have as many screenings,

00:08:15.729 --> 00:08:18.886
as many tests, and you do focus groups,

00:08:18.886 --> 00:08:20.026
and you read the cards,

00:08:20.026 --> 00:08:22.008
and you try to get a
peek of what they want,

00:08:22.008 --> 00:08:23.483
and that's comedy, man.

00:08:23.483 --> 00:08:25.582
- Where did the comedy part come in?

00:08:25.582 --> 00:08:27.353
Because you left high school

00:08:27.353 --> 00:08:30.461
to start a comedy career, didn't you?

00:08:30.461 --> 00:08:33.856
Was comedy like a way of
getting back at the bullies?

00:08:33.856 --> 00:08:35.287
Or where did it come from?

00:08:35.287 --> 00:08:37.021
- I always liked comedy.

00:08:37.021 --> 00:08:38.649
I was always interested in comedians,

00:08:38.649 --> 00:08:42.642
even when I was a kid in
second, I was seven years old.

00:08:42.642 --> 00:08:45.082
I thought Bill Cosby was unbelievable

00:08:45.082 --> 00:08:48.248
and I thought, you know, I
mean, Richard Pryor and John,

00:08:48.248 --> 00:08:50.110
all these guys, you know.

00:08:50.110 --> 00:08:53.367
I would watch the Dean Martin
Roast, and all of that stuff,

00:08:53.367 --> 00:08:55.034
Abbott and Costello.

00:08:59.403 --> 00:09:00.902
You know, at every point in my life,

00:09:00.902 --> 00:09:05.733
there's no point where I
wasn't obsessed with comedy.

00:09:05.733 --> 00:09:09.483
And I'm still obsessed
to this day, you know.

00:09:11.505 --> 00:09:14.730
So, you know, it was just a
natural thing for me to do.

00:09:14.730 --> 00:09:17.562
And anybody in this room
has ever been in love

00:09:17.562 --> 00:09:19.278
will testify to this shit.

00:09:19.278 --> 00:09:22.620
If you haven't contemplated
murder, you ain't been in love.

00:09:22.620 --> 00:09:24.586
(laughing)

00:09:24.586 --> 00:09:29.115
If you haven't (beep) thought
about killing a (beep),

00:09:29.115 --> 00:09:30.343
you ain't been in love.

00:09:30.343 --> 00:09:33.299
If you haven't had a can
of rat poison in your hand

00:09:33.299 --> 00:09:36.827
and looked at it for 45 minutes straight,

00:09:36.827 --> 00:09:38.488
you ain't been in love.

00:09:38.488 --> 00:09:41.668
If you haven't bought a shovel and a bag

00:09:41.668 --> 00:09:44.145
and a rug to roll they ass up in,

00:09:44.145 --> 00:09:45.714
you ain't been in love.

00:09:45.714 --> 00:09:50.507
If you haven't practiced your
alibi in front of the mirror,

00:09:50.507 --> 00:09:52.168
you ain't been in love.

00:09:52.168 --> 00:09:55.961
And the only thing that stops
you from killing this (beep)

00:09:55.961 --> 00:09:57.955
was a episode of CSI.

00:09:57.955 --> 00:10:01.455
(laughing and applauding)

00:10:06.071 --> 00:10:08.567
Oh man, they thorough.

00:10:08.567 --> 00:10:09.501
I better make up.

00:10:09.501 --> 00:10:10.749
They might catch my ass.

00:10:10.749 --> 00:10:11.980
(laughing)

00:10:11.980 --> 00:10:13.090
That's right, man.

00:10:13.090 --> 00:10:14.908
See, relationships are hard, man.

00:10:14.908 --> 00:10:17.419
But for order, for any
relationship to work,

00:10:17.419 --> 00:10:20.017
both people have to be on the same page.

00:10:20.017 --> 00:10:22.768
Both people have to have the same focus.

00:10:22.768 --> 00:10:24.261
We all know what that page is.

00:10:24.261 --> 00:10:25.803
We all know what that focus is.

00:10:25.803 --> 00:10:27.436
In order for the relationship to work,

00:10:27.436 --> 00:10:29.200
both people have to have the same focus.

00:10:29.200 --> 00:10:30.447
And what's that focus?

00:10:30.447 --> 00:10:32.697
The focus is all about her.

00:10:34.497 --> 00:10:36.080
It's all about her.

00:10:37.544 --> 00:10:39.309
